  "safety": "Browser actions: native Account GET and avatar-menu opening only, plus the capture helper GET used to verify the fictitious identity. Separately, the explicitly allowed account mutation was owner locale es→en→es through the protected Rails runner and User.update_columns(locale: l); restored Spanish is checked in DB and UI. Permission remains default, browser push subscription absent and Rails PushSubscription/PushNotification zero. The existing browser service worker is naturally registered/rechecked by the page; no notification/delivery worker executed. No forced/mocked permission/subscription/UI, Enable/Allow/Disable, other account or fixture change, messages/events, send/test/provider action. Measured fields equal after restoration; this does not claim no temporary mutation, whole-DB equality or last_online_at equality.",
